{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A carved figure.</b> Something hewn, like \"and Solomon's builders hewed\" (1 Kings 5:30)." "<b>Male or female.</b> Among the nations they are well-known. There are also nations that bow down and worship any animal they encounter at the start of their day, and some say to draw down the power of supernal beings in the form of a scorpion to bite, and the remaining forty-seven forms."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The phrase והצורות הארבעים ושבעה הנשארות is elliptical; translated hyper-literally without expanding what 'the remaining forty-seven forms' refers to."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:15.636705365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}